# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-16, R-6, RC-5; L §5.19 Readings at a place that keeps parts). L §5.19 Stated parts against booked parts: "a stated part is q's balance ... Where it differs from q's booked part,
# the difference is q's own gap: where positive, a part of q's of that amount ...; where negative, a take of q's parts by
# the leaving rule, its terms on w holes as above. The unstated rest has a gap of its own, over the labels the reading
# doesn't state, by the anchor's rules above".
# L §5.14.2: "a later reading's stated parts heal it". After the cycle of observed rows (L5_14_2_cycle_observed),
# konto's anchor at the day's end states b1 70.00 and b2 20.00 of 90.00: each stated part is its batch's balance, and
# the unstated rest (0.00 against the hole part's 90.00) takes the hole part whole, so konto's batches are known again;
# konto2's aren't (scratch/exp7.py).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind lots: place PLN min 0
  batched
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order k.batch.day
input bank: observed
place konto: lots lives 2026-01-01..
place konto2: lots lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input b1_day: date
input b1_amt: money PLN
input b2_day: date
input b2_amt: money PLN
move b1: transfers
  on b1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount b1_amt
move b2: transfers
  on b2_day
  leg cash from world to konto2 amount b2_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-01), bal(konto, 2026-03-01) of b1, bal(konto2, 2026-03-01), bal(konto2, 2026-03-01) of b2

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[konto2] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  b1_day = 2026-02-01
  b1_amt = 100.00 PLN
  b2_day = 2026-02-15
  b2_amt = 50.00 PLN
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-03-01, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to konto2 amount 30.00 PLN) "r1"
  bank[r2] = (on: 2026-03-01, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto2 to konto amount 20.00 PLN) "r2"

version stmt
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-04-01
  anchor konto
  stated[konto] = 90.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 end
  stated[konto] of b1 = 70.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 end
  stated[konto] of b2 = 20.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 end
=== expect
q: (90.00 PLN, 70.00 PLN, 60.00 PLN, ?"konto2: 60.00 PLN may be b2's: which of bank[r1], bank[r2] went first on 2026-03-01?" (konto2))
  anchor: konto 2026-03-01 end, stated 90.00 PLN, difference 0.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: b2
  cut 2026-10-01
